"The battery guard — which stops Keep Awake from running a session down to empty — now starts on for new installs, at 20%. It shipped off by default, beside a session length that defaults to indefinite." = "The battery guard — which stops Keep Awake from running a session down to empty — now starts on for new installs, at 20%. It shipped off by default, beside a session length that defaults to indefinite.";
"The disk is full. Moving to the Trash needs room, because the Trash is a folder on the same disk — empty it and try again." = "The disk is full. Moving to the Trash needs room, because the Trash is a folder on the same disk — empty it and try again.";
"The disk list can be walked from the keyboard: arrow keys between rows, Return to go into a folder, ⌘↑ to come back out. And the screen now fits the width it has: on a narrow window the ring gives way to the list, which carries the same facts in less room." = "The disk list can be walked from the keyboard: arrow keys between rows, Return to go into a folder, ⌘↑ to come back out. And the screen now fits the width it has: on a narrow window the ring gives way to the list, which carries the same facts in less room.";
"The disk map now answers VoiceOver: every wedge reads its name, its size and its share of the folder, and can be opened from there. Folders in the list beside it can be opened from the context menu too — the double-click still works and is no longer the only way." = "The disk map now answers VoiceOver: every wedge reads its name, its size and its share of the folder, and can be opened from there. Folders in the list beside it can be opened from the context menu too — the double-click still works and is no longer the only way.";
"The disk ring grows into the folder you opened. It shows three levels at a time, and the level that arrived when you drilled in had nowhere to come from — it appeared all at once at the end of the animation. Now it slides in with the rest." = "The disk ring grows into the folder you opened. It shows three levels at a time, and the level that arrived when you drilled in had nowhere to come from — it appeared all at once at the end of the animation. Now it slides in with the rest.";
"The disk ring was measuring the wrong thing when you scanned a folder: it drew the volume's free space alongside the folder's contents, so a small folder came out as a blank grey circle. And “Scan again” now scans the same place again instead of sending you back to the volume list. In the duplicate finder, files that refused to move stay ticked, so you can fix the reason and try again without starting over. Homebrew search puts the name you typed first." = "The disk ring was measuring the wrong thing when you scanned a folder: it drew the volume's free space alongside the folder's contents, so a small folder came out as a blank grey circle. And “Scan again” now scans the same place again instead of sending you back to the volume list. In the duplicate finder, files that refused to move stay ticked, so you can fix the reason and try again without starting over. Homebrew search puts the name you typed first.";
"The disk this is on is read-only. Eject it and unlock it, or copy what you need elsewhere." = "The disk this is on is read-only. Eject it and unlock it, or copy what you need elsewhere.";
"The download did not match what the release published, so Helm did not install it." = "The download did not match what the release published, so Helm did not install it.";
"The duplicate finder is its own screen now, right after Disk. It used to search whatever folder the ring happened to be showing, so you could only look where you had already scanned; now you point it at a folder and it remembers it. It still compares content rather than names, still keeps one copy of every group, and still never offers a hard link." = "The duplicate finder is its own screen now, right after Disk. It used to search whatever folder the ring happened to be showing, so you could only look where you had already scanned; now you point it at a folder and it remembers it. It still compares content rather than names, still keeps one copy of every group, and still never offers a hard link.";
"The duplicate finder no longer holds on to everything it reads. It compares files a megabyte at a time so a video never has to fit in memory — but the app kept every one of those megabytes until the scan ended, so the memory it used followed the size of the folder rather than the size of a slice. The background check for updates had the same defect in its own file check. Memory is also handed back to macOS when a scan finishes and when a module is switched off, instead of being kept for later." = "The duplicate finder no longer holds on to everything it reads. It compares files a megabyte at a time so a video never has to fit in memory — but the app kept every one of those megabytes until the scan ended, so the memory it used followed the size of the folder rather than the size of a slice. The background check for updates had the same defect in its own file check. Memory is also handed back to macOS when a scan finishes and when a module is switched off, instead of being kept for later.";
"The file is locked, or you are not its owner. Open Get Info in the Finder to unlock it or change its permissions." = "The file is locked, or you are not its owner. Open Get Info in the Finder to unlock it or change its permissions.";
"The icon is white when idle and takes on the colour of whichever module is active." = "The icon is white when idle and takes on the colour of whichever module is active.";
"The icon shape, icon size and both colours can be chosen from the keyboard, and Escape leaves the shortcut recorder." = "The icon shape, icon size and both colours can be chosen from the keyboard, and Escape leaves the shortcut recorder.";
"The log Helm keeps for troubleshooting no longer writes down the names of your VPN connections, your apps, or the path to your home folder." = "The log Helm keeps for troubleshooting no longer writes down the names of your VPN connections, your apps, or the path to your home folder.";
"The log records what Helm did, not what you have: app names, VPN names and paths are replaced before anything is written." = "The log records what Helm did, not what you have: app names, VPN names and paths are replaced before anything is written.";
"The menu-bar countdown ticks reliably; heavy work no longer stalls the app’s async machinery." = "The menu-bar countdown ticks reliably; heavy work no longer stalls the app’s async machinery.";
"The module order you set is now used everywhere — the panel, the sidebar in Settings, and the icon’s menu — and it no longer gets lost when a drag is abandoned." = "The module order you set is now used everywhere — the panel, the sidebar in Settings, and the icon’s menu — and it no longer gets lost when a drag is abandoned.";
"The panel no longer jumps or slides when sections expand; settings stay in sync between the panel and the Settings window." = "The panel no longer jumps or slides when sections expand; settings stay in sync between the panel and the Settings window.";
"The slower update channel is called Beta, not Stable. Helm has not reached 1.0, and nothing shipped so far has earned the word stable — the app says Beta on its About page for the same reason." = "The slower update channel is called Beta, not Stable. Helm has not reached 1.0, and nothing shipped so far has earned the word stable — the app says Beta on its About page for the same reason.";
